<blockquote>
<p>That said, does the story itself at least sound compelling?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Personally I'm lukewarm on it. The general gist seems to just be &quot;human is stuck in a different world and at the whim of a distressed deity like figure, eventually escapes&quot;. I myself am uncertain what the reader is supposed to take away from the story besides &quot;it sucks to be the characters in this story&quot;. There's a lot of specific details about what these individuals end up doing, but the guy just escaping at the end doesn't feel super meaningful or impactful for me. I would probably want to see the guy convince the deity to let him go or to help him find a way to leave. Maybe he leaves something in that world and promises to return. Maybe he takes something with him in exchange. Something more than just &quot;guy conveniently manages to get out of there, the end&quot;.</p>

							</div>

								
					
