<blockquote>
<p>If the world is one contiguous ocean, how would you specifically account for salinity, temperature, pH level… especially if the world is deserted?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's otherworldly, created by thaumaturgists, meant to potentially welcome species from all over the universe, and not related to Earth, presumably? Must it conform to Earth's physics? Again, this is a worldbuilding question from me; you seem to want to have the world be both not related to Earth but still reliant on a lot of Earth-specific properties. Again, you can proceed that way if you really want to, but there should be a good in-universe reason for that besides &quot;I am the author and I want it that way&quot;.</p>

