														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852328">
									

<p>I dunno. I don't see having a freshwater sea as very contrived. If anything, engineering entire pockets of the world - which, again, is almost entirely oceanic - seems far more unreasonable in my mind. If the world is one contiguous ocean, how would you specifically account for salinity, temperature, pH level&#8230; especially if the world is deserted? There's no one there to maintain the delicate balance of the separate biomes, which in my opinion raises far more questions than simply having available fresh water.</p>

							</div>

								
					
